C/ EXCLUSIVE procedure mutual exclusion (USA003087 Sec. 27.2): the RTE
C/ allows only one process to use P at a time.  The primal CALLs P and
C/ WAITs mid-body (still holding it); the DEPENDENT task B, running during
C/ that WAIT, tries to CALL P and is BLOCKED until the primal leaves P and
C/ releases the reservation.  Because B is DEPENDENT, the primal's CLOSE
C/ waits for it (Sec. 13.3), so B is then granted P and runs it to
C/ completion.  The two ENTER P/LEAVE P pairs are fully serialized (never
C/ overlapping) -- and both CALLs return to the right place ("B GOT P"),
C/ which a non-serialized barge-in would corrupt (shared interpreter call
C/ stack).  Expected: BEFORE / ENTER P / B TRY P / LEAVE P / PRIMAL DONE /
C/ ENTER P / LEAVE P / B GOT P.
 TEXCL2: PROGRAM;
    P: PROCEDURE EXCLUSIVE;
       WRITE(6) 'ENTER P';
       WAIT 1.0;
       WRITE(6) 'LEAVE P';
    CLOSE P;
    B: TASK;
       WRITE(6) 'B TRY P';
       CALL P;
       WRITE(6) 'B GOT P';
    CLOSE B;
    WRITE(6) 'BEFORE';
    SCHEDULE B PRIORITY(80) DEPENDENT;
    CALL P;
    WRITE(6) 'PRIMAL DONE';
 CLOSE TEXCL2;
